   "subject": "geom_nodepoint remains in same place despite flip",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi there.</div><div>First of all thanks for creating the ggtree package!</div><div>I am running R code as such:</div><div>r &lt;- ggtree(BS1000, size=0.05) + geom_tiplab(align=TRUE, linetype = NULL, size=1) + geom_treescale(offset = 3, linesize = 0.2, fontsize = 2, y= 50, x=0.002) + geom_nodepoint(data=d, size = 1)<br>r<br>s &lt;- flip(r,165,240)<br>s</div><div>In the first instance the geom_nodepoints are nicely plotted as they should be, but after I flip certain branches around the geom_nodepoints layer stays the same and does not adjust to the new orientation of the branches. How can I fix this issue?</div><div>Thanks.</div><div>Tim<br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
