     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Mon, Oct 29, 2018 at 7:57 PM Tim HH <a href=\"http://mailto:tim...@posteo.de\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mailto:tim...@posteo.de&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482394571000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_OiL11HudkLSO01YNOxQG\">ti...@posteo.de</a> wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi there.</div><div>First of all thanks for creating the ggtree package!</div><div>I am running R code as such:</div><div>r &lt;- ggtree(BS1000, size=0.05) + geom_tiplab(align=TRUE, linetype = NULL, size=1) + geom_treescale(offset = 3, linesize = 0.2, fontsize = 2, y= 50, x=0.002) + geom_nodepoint(data=d, size = 1)<br>r<br>s &lt;- flip(r,165,240)<br>s</div><div>In the first instance the geom_nodepoints are nicely plotted as they should be, but after I flip certain branches around the geom_nodepoints layer stays the same and does not adjust to the new orientation of the branches. How can I fix this issue?</div><div>Thanks.</div><div>Tim<br></div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div></div>"
