   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I see. <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">d</code> contained a subset with node numbers that had a bootstrap above a certain threshold. I am now using + geom_point2(aes(label=label, subset=!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482394575000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ZjL-0LUxkUX7cpZOIGXhU\">is.na</a>(as.numeric(label)) &amp; label &gt;70)) instead, which does the trick.</div><div>Thanks.<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Tuesday, October 30, 2018 at 1:55:21 AM UTC+1, Yu, Guangchuang wrote:</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">&gt; x = rtree(30)                    \r\n&gt; ggtree(x) + geom_nodepoint() -&gt; p\r\n&gt; flip(p, 48, 59)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">The above code works without any problem.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You issue is due to the data <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">d</code> in <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">geom_nodepoint(data=d, size = 1)</code>. </p>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Mon, Oct 29, 2018 at 7:57 PM Tim HH wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p><div><p></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi there.</div><div>First of all thanks for creating the ggtree package!</div><div>I am running R code as such:</div><div>r &lt;- ggtree(BS1000, size=0.05) + geom_tiplab(align=TRUE, linetype = NULL, size=1) + geom_treescale(offset = 3, linesize = 0.2, fontsize = 2, y= 50, x=0.002) + geom_nodepoint(data=d, size = 1)<br>r<br>s &lt;- flip(r,165,240)<br>s</div><div>In the first instance the geom_nodepoints are nicely plotted as they should be, but after I flip certain branches around the geom_nodepoints layer stays the same and does not adjust to the new orientation of the branches. How can I fix this issue?</div><div>Thanks.</div><div>Tim<br></div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nG Yu, DK Smith, H Zhu, Y Guan, TTY Lam*. ggtree: an R package for visualization and annotation of phylogenetic trees with their covariates and other associated data, Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 2017, 8(1):28-36. doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12628<br>\r\n <br>\r\nHomepage: <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482394575000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Fg1-aZL4qS9vtq-Elx1x2\">https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggtree&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel